# A template for the development PDS's env file (P1.29a). Every value here is a placeholder. Copy it to
# ../unset-dev-env/pds.env (beside this checkout, 0600, owned by you), then set real values there; no live env file
# lives in the checkout (record 2026-10-12-p127u-bind-ancestors-and-build-context, Amendments 2 and 3). The PDS takes
# its settings only from its environment (@atproto/pds 0.5.37 dist/config/env.js), so its secrets come through this
# file, not /run/secrets. It holds only these names: every other PDS setting is a literal in compose.dev.yaml, which
# Compose prefers over env_file (compose_dev_pds_env_file_holds_only_its_secrets). One env per host: under local it
# holds the first four names only, under dev and prod all six (preflight P1.36q). The runbook
# docs/human/runbooks/dev-stack-secrets.md says how to make each value.

# The session token signing secret: openssl rand -hex 32.
PDS_JWT_SECRET=replace-me
# The admin password, at least 32 characters (P1.30 C7): openssl rand -hex 32.
PDS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-me
# The PLC rotation key: a secp256k1 private key as 64 hex characters (the runbook gives the command).
PDS_PLC_ROTATION_KEY_K256_PRIVATE_KEY_HEX=replace-me
# The recovery did:key (public; its private half stays offline with Alex): set before the first account (P1.30 C6).
PDS_RECOVERY_DID_KEY=replace-me
# dev and prod only: the account mail URL, smtps with the mail key as its password (C11; the from address is a
# compose literal). Leave this line out under local, which sends no mail.
PDS_EMAIL_SMTP_URL=replace-me
# dev and prod only: the moderation mail URL, under C11's rule (C19). A separate key is recommended; the same works.
PDS_MODERATION_EMAIL_SMTP_URL=replace-me
